items(S, "guide_section",
      ["What egress lighting is for", "When normal power fails, people still need to find the way out. Exit signs mark the route; emergency lights make it visible. Both have to work on their own power."],
      ["Battery duration and testing", "Battery-backed units are commonly required to run for 90 minutes. Batteries wear out, which is why regular testing matters more than the fixture itself."],
      ["Older Chicago buildings", "Walk-up and courtyard buildings often have long corridors and stairs fed by few circuits. Adding units sometimes means adding an unswitched supply, which is the part that takes time."],
      ["Inspection notices", "A notice lists specific items. Correcting exactly those, and recording the tests, is the fastest route to a passed re-inspection."])
